course: dictionary
lesson: 14717
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Production» is a good example. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «The factory's production of toys rose by 200 a day.» Here production means the amount that is made. The clue is rose by 200 a day, which is about numbers, so it must mean how much is made.
explain: «The school production was great fun.» Here production means a play or show put on for people. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A play or a show fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it. If not, try the next meaning and keep reading.
fact: Production means making or growing things, especially in large amounts, such as «car production» or «food production».
fact: Production can also mean the amount that is made, as in «Production rose by 200 tins a day».
fact: «The school production» means a play, show or film that is put on for people.
fact: In a formal way, «on production of a ticket» means when you show a ticket.
fact: Useful phrases include «in production», «go into production» and «mass production».
exercise: «Production rose by 200 tins a day.» What does production mean here? | A play put on for people | Showing a ticket at the door | *The amount that is made | A kind of farm
exercise: A factory makes 40 toys an hour. This is a production problem: how many toys in 8 hours? | 400 | *320 | 48 | 240
exercise: «The school production of Annie is on Friday night.» What does production mean here? | The number of tins made each day | *A play or show put on for people | Making things in a factory | Growing food on a farm
test: «Car production is up this year.» What does car production mean? | *Making cars in large amounts, as in a factory | A show about cars | Driving cars to school | Making cars in large amounts
test: «Entry is on production of a ticket.» What does on production mean? | *When you show something | After the show ends | When you make something | When you lose something
exam: Which phrase means making things in very large amounts, often by machines? | on production of | *mass production | in the park | the school production
